  {
    "index": 14,
    "hash": "Zfjmgw+Wxu+Emq1jiSodj/T6uvw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:59:23.935Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The v6 Reactor provides `RelationalDbProcessor<DB>` as a base class for processors that need database access. Key features: `getNamespace(driveId)` static method creates per-drive database isolation preventing data collisions; `initAndUpgrade()` lifecycle hook runs migrations on startup; `this.relationalDb` provides a typed Kysely instance; `query(driveId, relationalDb)` static method enables querying from subgraphs. The factory creates namespaced stores via `module.relationalDb.createNamespace<T>(namespace)`. Scaffolding is generated with `ph generate processor --name <name> --type relationalDb --document-types <type>`.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._\n\n## Correction at v6.2.2-dev.74\n\"Lifecycle management\" overstates what the base class does about migrations. At v6.2.2-dev.74 the generated template makes migrations the processor's own responsibility:\n\n```ts\nexport class MyProcessor extends RelationalDbProcessor<DB> {\n  override async initAndUpgrade(): Promise<void> { await up(this.relationalDb); }\n}\n```\n\nSo there is no automatic discovery of a migrations folder \u2014 `initAndUpgrade` is the hook, and the processor calls its own `up`. Per-drive namespace isolation (`static getNamespace(driveId)`, defaulting to `${this.name}_${driveId.replaceAll(\"-\",\"_\")}`) and the type-safe Kysely surface are unchanged.\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:59:23.935Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:59:23.935Z"
    }
  }
